            <ArticleTitle>Mesenteric ischemia after a cardiac operation: arteriosclerotic versus vasospastic etiology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastrointestinal complications after extracorporeal circulation are rare but well known complications. We describe and illustrate 2 patients with occlusive intestinal ischemia of different origin presenting after cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) and present the different therapeutic algorithm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
